  "title": "Permutation in String",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Sliding window",
  "patterns": [
    "sliding window",
    "fixed-size window"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "a permutation of s1 has a fixed length and a fixed set of letter counts. what kind of window are you looking for in s2?",
    "build a frequency count of s1's letters once, then slide a same-size window across s2, maintaining a frequency count of the window's letters",
    "as the window slides by one, only two letters change: the one leaving and the one entering - update counts incrementally instead of rebuilding them",
    "at each position, check if the window's frequency count exactly matches s1's frequency count"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "recomputing the whole frequency count for every window position instead of updating it incrementally",
    "comparing sorted substrings, which works but is slower than tracking counts directly",
    "off-by-one on the window size, or forgetting to check the very last possible window position"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two strings, `s1` and `s2`.\n\n**Determine whether `s2` contains a contiguous substring that is a permutation (rearrangement) of `s1`.**\n\nA permutation of `s1` uses exactly the same letters, with the same counts, in any order.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= s1.length <= 10^4",
      "1 <= s2.length <= 10^4",
      "s1 and s2 consist only of lowercase English letters"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "s1 is longer than s2 (always false)",
      "s1 equals s2 exactly",
      "s2 contains repeated letters that overlap with s1's letters in confusing ways"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s1 = \"ab\", s2 = \"eidbaooo\"",
        "output": "true",
        "expectedOutput": "true",
        "explanation": "\"ba\" inside eidbaooo uses exactly the letters a and b, a permutation of \"ab\""
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
